cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PhenoCleaning: an auditable pipeline for 3D multispectral plant-phenotyping time-series"
abstract: >-
  An auditable, design-agnostic pipeline that turns the raw outputs of a Phenospex PlantEye /
  TraitFinder scanner (tabular exports and 3D point clouds) into a clean, quality-controlled,
  analysis-ready dataset. It reconciles multiple exports, encodes quality-control and missing-data
  checks, handles irregular-timing time-series without imputation, and offers geometry-based
  soil/pot-rim removal and per-plant spectral rendering. All curation is user-driven and
  non-destructive.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Agyeya
    family-names: Pratap
    affiliation: "Australian Plant Phenomics Network, The University of Western Australia"
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
